// The desk's policy (PS8, PT8; the concierge's policy is its model). An email change waits for a person, who approves it with a
// signed record (PF9.6); the Desk's `sensitive` field says the write in flight is an email change. A phone or address change
// is not matched, so the gate allows it. The guard proposal.kind == "effect" keeps the rule off the proposals that are not
// effects, where effect is unknown. No never statement: S149 reads an escalation an approval would allow as an allow.
module desk_policy

policy changes {
  scope "desk"
  obligation email-change-reviewed "An email change is made only after a person approves it." rule {
    when proposal.kind == "effect" && effect.kind == "customers.write" && machine("desk.Desk").sensitive
    require false else escalate
    on unknown escalate
  }
}
